method.description:
Collects writes inside [param body] and commits them as one batch.
[param body] receives a [NetwTransaction] and calls [method NetwTransaction.queue_upsert] for each record to write. The commit runs once [param body] returns, which is what makes it happen exactly once however the body exits.
The promise settles with an [enum @GlobalScope.Error] rather than rejecting, which is what [method NetwDatabaseBackend.commit] itself does: in this layer a refused write is an ordinary answer, and a caller reads the code off [member NetwPromise.result]. [signal transaction_committed] announces only a commit that answered [constant @GlobalScope.OK], since a promise that settled is not the same thing as a write that landed.
[codeblock]
var err: Error = await db.transaction(
    func(tx: NetwTransaction) -> void:
        tx.queue_upsert(&"rocks", &"rock_1", {&"health": 50})
).wait()
[/codeblock]
A caller that must not suspend, such as a pump that would let its next round start inside this one, chains [method NetwPromise.then] on the same answer instead of awaiting it.
